---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const skillGroups = [
  {
    title: "Build with",
    items: ["Python", "JavaScript", "Node.js", "Git", "VS Code", "GitHub Copilot", "Claude"],
  },
  {
    title: "Work with",
    items: ["Power BI", "Azure DevOps", "Jira", "Confluence", "Agile / Scrum"],
  },
  {
    title: "Currently advancing in",
    items: ["SQL", "Tableau"],
  },
];
---
<Layout title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I'm Amina Lawal. I love data, AI and communication.
    My path has no straight line, but it has a pattern: wherever I've worked, I've ended up in the space between the people who know a thing and the people who need it.
    I started in radio, managing live broadcasts, then transitioned to IT and data.
    The thread through my work has been taking something complicated and making it understandable for the people who have to act on it.
    I'm looking for an entry-level role where I can work between technical and non-technical people.
    I'm looking for a role where I can work at the intersection of AI, data, and communication — somewhere that values clear reasoning, thorough documentation, and picking the right tool for the job, even when that tool isn't (all) AI.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="skills-heading">
    <h2 id="skills-heading">What I work with</h2>
    {skillGroups.map((group) => (
      <div>
        <h3>{group.title}</h3>
        <ul>
          {group.items.map((item) => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>
</Layout>